TypeScript 7 (the native Go port of tsc) reports "No overload matches this
call" at the offending argument, not at the start of the call as TypeScript 6
does. The two @ts-expect-error directives sit above `this.bind_property_full(`
with the argument on the next line, so under TypeScript 7 they suppress
nothing and the build fails with TS2578 + TS2769.

Putting the first argument on the call's own line makes the directive cover
the error under both compilers. Code is unchanged.

--- gnome-weather-50.0/src/app/thermometer.ts
+++ gnome-weather-50.0/src/app/thermometer.ts
@@ -290,8 +290,7 @@
         // @ts-expect-error ts-for-gir does not `bind_property_full` correctly. In GJS it actually returns a
         // tuple of [boolean, value] where the boolean is whether the transformation succeeded, and the value
         // is the transformed value.
-        this.bind_property_full(
-            'range',
+        this.bind_property_full('range',
             this.lowLabel,
             'label',
             GObject.BindingFlags.DEFAULT,
@@ -302,8 +301,7 @@
         );
 
         // @ts-expect-error Same as the above.
-        this.bind_property_full(
-            'range',
+        this.bind_property_full('range',
             this.highLabel,
             'label',
             GObject.BindingFlags.DEFAULT,
